    "q-119692": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119692",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/0a6b6f6ef3902dc1dcd60ca6c5314befd6e8b3ca7c23d74145d17d1285e7f025.png)\n\nWhat regular polyhedron is shown in the picture above?",
      "worked_solution": "The picture shows an *icosahedron*, a convex regular polyhedron that  \n\n- consists of $20$ congruent faces, each in the form of an equilateral triangle, and\n\n- exactly $5$ faces meet at each vertex.\n\nRecall that there are only five types of Platonic solids (convex regular polyhedra):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/bc67deabe1622e7ac3015c3ec942f254e59c58f406e026c367e0c0aeee5a6d3e.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
