    "q-119706": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119706",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following is an octahedron?",
      "worked_solution": "Among the given options, the *octahedron* is shown in the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/ca522caf67546fca79cc3edccf0cd1b3f82b7a42205e5721a9a5a305792471e9.png)\n\n \n\nAn octahedron is a regular polyhedron that \n\n- consists of $8$ congruent faces, each in the form of an equilateral triangle, and\n\n- exactly $4$ faces meet at each vertex.\n\nRecall that there are only five types of Platonic solids (convex regular polyhedra):\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/bc67deabe1622e7ac3015c3ec942f254e59c58f406e026c367e0c0aeee5a6d3e.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-119706-a",
              "type": "image",
              "value": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/d6076b0a7e18cd261fcdff25ec3bb44e8314f2316c51398aac32721fe2398ad3.png",
              "html": "<img src=\"/graphics/q-119706-a-3\">",
              "source_url": "https://mathacademy.com/graphics/q-119706-a-3",
              "source_urls": [
                "https://mathacademy.com/graphics/q-119706-a-3"
