    "q-119784": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119784",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. A tetrahedron has $4$ congruent faces, each in the form of an equilateral triangle\n\nII. An octahedron has $12$ congruent faces, each in the form of an equilateral triangle\n\nIII. A dodecahedron has $12$ congruent faces, each in the form of an equilateral triangle",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14268510/assets/bc67deabe1622e7ac3015c3ec942f254e59c58f406e026c367e0c0aeee5a6d3e.png)\n\n \n\nLet's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. A tetrahedron has $4$ congruent faces, where each face is an equilateral triangle.\n\n- Statement II is false. An octahedron is a regular polyhedron consisting of $8$ (not $12$) congruent faces, where each face is an equilateral triangle.\n\n- Statement III is false. A dodecahedron is a regular polyhedron consisting of $12$ congruent faces, where each face is a regular pentagon (not an equilateral triangle).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
